Last week (I'm a slow poster) Angantyr the Elf at last entered
demigodhood after 110551 moves (why hurry?) and with 3500576 points.
  Stats 18/**, 18, 18, 20, 20, 11 with +2 GoD (I was strong enough anyway)
and +2 HoB; HP 255 and Pw 211.
His treasure was limited to 7 emeralds, 3 jade stones and 1 aquamarine
as he accidently forgot his sack of gems on level 17 (and didn't
remember it until it was too late).
  He also carried one AoLS (and had forgotten one somewhere in
Gehennom), 28 potions of holy water and loads of scrolls of
teleportation, remove curse and charging. Several useful wands too,
including the Castle WoW with 2+1 wishes left. As I've never come as
far as to meed the Wiz before, I guess I was a bit over-cautious. And
I never got around to take my wands out of my bag.
Note that the only weapon I carried after having defeated Vlad was the
+6 Stormy - why are people screaming about not being able to throw
Mjollnir safely?

Debated features used included polypiling, reverse-genociding of
tengus (that did NOT give me any teleport control) and giants (get
strong fast) and a few ordinary wishes, but no wishing for artifacts
(including weapons), no cursed bell trick and certainly no save file
duplication. I even didn't use Nurse services, but on the other hand I
jumped in the arms of every Succubus I saw which proved very
rewarding.

Killed were 3653 creatures, including the demon lords (a little
accident there with Yeenoghu; I didn't plan to kill him but Stormy has
its features...), Famine (I never saw the other riders) and the
Wiz*10. Only *one* Archon though, where did they go?
Genocided L's (the first scroll was blessed), Rust monsters (hate!),
Soldiers (I had one spare scroll and wanted to know what the Castle
would contain without them (answer: mostly o's (Zzzzzz))) and ;'s, but
not until I enterer the Wiz's tower.

The keys to success this time were:
* The little kitten Satan was polymorphed into a Water Elemental on
  the first mine level. He then served well until he at last was lost
  to a dragon (I think) in Ludios.
* An early GDSM, from a bones level.
* Many AoLS, in fact five and that was without any wishing. But they
  were needed; I used three of them. First early in the game when I
  was killed by a Black Pudding while fainting (stupid), then I was
  stoned by a cockatrice in the Wiz's tower (even more stupid; where
  were my lizard corpses?) and last time on the Astral Plane when
  Famine got me fainting after one touch...
* Two lucky early wishes from water demons. On the other hand I have
  *never* got a wish from sitting on a throne.
* Firebrand was just lying around in the store in the Minetown.
* I got my hands (with gloves, of course :-) on a cockatrice corpse
  just before I entered the Astral Plane. VERY useful.
* No Archons on the Astral Plane. 

On the other hand...
* No randomly generated Wands of Death - the only one in the game was
  Orcus'. And I did quite a lot of polypiling...
* Only one randomly generated magic marker. Booo.
* I had to wish for a BoH with the Castle WoW (which was the only one
  BTW, but I'm not complaining about *that*). On the other hand the
  mazes in Gehennom had three of them just lying there.

Critical moments:
* The three deaths of course.
* Cornered by three Jabberwocks at Juiblex's. Close.
* In the Sanctum, with double-troubled Wiz, tons of mad priests and I
  had dropped my bag with all my equipment on some unknown sqare
  covered by a corpse.
* The Astral Plane. I had entered it wearing a RoC, and things looked
  bad for a while even though I didn't meet a single Archon. But I
  like it, the end should be hard.

Way too wimpy:
* The Elves' quest. Just killing o's!? This was third time I was there,
  and it was just boring.
* Vlad. I've been visiting him once before and then I cleared his
  tower with a pick-axe. This time I remembered to wield Stormy and it
  was no match at all. He didn't even fight back!?
* Where were those Archons again?


One question:
I've heard people say that walking up through Gehennom is much easier if
you're chaothic.
I've also heard people tell horror stories about being teleported down a
all the time when they climb up the stairs to the next level. I was only
teleported to other places on the same level. 

